enum LibrarySnapshot {
    static let lines: [String] = [
        "Beam front squat\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes, core\tBeam across the collarbones. Three counts down, one to stand.\tThe beam across the collarbones, resting on the front of the shoulders, elbows lifted, feet a little wider than the hips.¦Sit down over three counts with the chest tall, then stand in one.¦Thighs and glutes; the upper back works to keep the beam up.¦Letting the elbows drop so the beam rolls forward; keep the elbows up and the chest proud.¦Sharp knee pain or a wrist that cannot tolerate the beam\'s position.",
        "Beam deadlift\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\thinge\t0\tglutes, back, legs\tHinge from the hips. The beam stays close to your shins.\tThe beam on the floor against the shins, feet hip width, hands just outside the legs.¦Push the hips back, take the beam, and stand up tall keeping it close to the legs the whole way.¦Hamstrings load on the way down; standing up is the glutes.¦Letting the beam drift forward away from the shins, which pulls on the low back.¦The back rounds or you feel it in the spine rather than the legs.",
        "Beam good morning\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\thinge\t0\tglutes, back\tThe beam rests across the back of the shoulders, never the neck. Soft knees, flat back, stop when your hamstrings say so.\tThe beam across the back of the shoulders, never on the neck, feet hip width, knees soft.¦Hinge forward from the hips with a flat back until the hamstrings stop you, then stand.¦A stretch down the back of the thighs; the glutes bring you back up.¦Rounding the back to go lower; the range is whatever your hamstrings allow with a flat back.¦Any pinch in the low back — this move has no business there.",
        "Beam hip thrust\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tcoreExtension\t2\tglutes\tOn your back on the mat, beam across the hips. Press through the heels and hold a beat at the top.\tOn your back on the mat, knees bent, the beam across the hips held in both hands.¦Drive through the heels to lift the hips, hold a beat at the top, and lower slowly.¦The glutes.¦Arching the back at the top; tuck the ribs and let the glutes finish.¦Low back pain.",
        "Beam overhead press\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tFrom the collarbones to straight overhead. Ribs stay down as the arms go up.\tThe beam across the collarbones, hands shoulder width, ribs down.¦Press straight up until the arms are by the ears, then lower to the collarbones.¦Shoulders and the back of the arms.¦Pressing out in front rather than straight up; move the head back slightly and let the beam travel in a straight line.¦Shoulder pinch or the low back arching to help.",
        "Beam row\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tback, arms\tHinge and hold it there. Pull the beam to your belly, elbows back not out.\tHinge forward with a flat back, the beam hanging at arm\'s length, hands shoulder width.¦Pull the beam to the belly, elbows back, squeeze the shoulder blades, lower slowly.¦Between and below the shoulder blades.¦Standing up to meet the beam; the torso stays still and the beam comes to you.¦Low back pain rather than upper back work.",
        "Beam reverse lunge\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\tsides\tlunge\t0\tlegs, glutes\tBeam across the chest. Step back, and the front knee stays over the ankle.\tThe beam across the chest or the front of the shoulders, feet under the hips.¦Step back, lower the back knee toward the floor, and drive through the front heel to stand.¦Front thigh and glute; the core holds the beam still.¦The front knee drifting past the toes; keep it over the ankle.¦Sharp knee pain or balance so poor the beam is moving.",
        "Beam floor press\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t2\tchest, arms\tOn your back, beam at the chest, press straight up. The floor stops your elbows.\tOn your back, knees bent, the beam held over the chest with the upper arms on the floor.¦Press straight up, pause, and lower until the elbows meet the floor.¦Chest and the back of the arms.¦Bouncing the elbows off the floor; touch and press.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Beam overhead hold\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\tcarry\t0\tcore, shoulders\tThe beam pressed overhead, arms by the ears. Ribs down over the hips, and hold.\tThe beam pressed overhead, arms long beside the ears, ribs down.¦Hold it still and breathe.¦The shoulders and the core keeping the ribs down.¦The low back arching as the arms tire; lower the beam before that happens.¦Shoulder pinch or any arching.",
        "Beam curl\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tBoth hands under the beam, elbows pinned to your sides. Curl to the collarbones, three counts down.\tStanding tall, both hands under the beam, elbows pinned to the sides.¦Curl to the collarbones and lower over three counts.¦The front of the upper arms.¦Leaning back to lift; stay tall.¦Elbow or wrist pain.",
        "Beam triceps extension\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\t\taccessory\t2\tarms\tOn your back, the beam pressed over the chest. Bend only the elbows, lower it toward your forehead, press back up.\tOn your back, the beam pressed over the chest, hands shoulder width.¦Bend only the elbows to lower it toward the forehead, then straighten.¦The back of the upper arms.¦The upper arms moving; they stay vertical.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Beam lateral lunge\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\tsides\tlunge\t0\tlegs, glutes\tBeam across the collarbones. Step wide to one side, sit into that hip, and push back to standing.\tThe beam across the collarbones, feet together.¦Step wide to one side, sit back into that hip with the other leg straight, then push back to standing.¦The glute and inner thigh of the bent leg.¦The bent knee falling inward; keep it over the foot and the chest up.¦Sharp knee or groin pain.",
        "Beam curtsy lunge\tbeam\tstrength\t15.0\tsides\tlunge\t0\tglutes, legs\tBeam across the collarbones. Step back and across, sink straight down; the front knee stays steady.\tThe beam across the collarbones, feet under the hips.¦Step one foot back and across behind the other, sink straight down, and stand.¦The outer glute of the front leg.¦Twisting the hips; they stay square to the front.¦Any knee pain on the front leg.",
        "Ring halo\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tdirections\tcoreAntiRotation\t0\tshoulders, arms, core\tThe 5 lb ring in both hands, slow circles around the head.\tThe 5 lb ring held in both hands in front of the face, feet hip width, ribs down.¦Circle the ring slowly around the head, close to it, one way and then the other.¦The shoulders, and the core keeping you from swaying.¦Bending the neck to get the ring round; the head stays still and the arms travel.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Ring press-out\trings\tstrength\t8.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t0\tchest, shoulders, core\tHold the 8 lb ring at the chest and press straight out.\tThe 8 lb ring held at the chest in both hands, feet hip width.¦Press the ring straight out in front until the arms are long, hold a beat, and bring it back.¦The chest and front of the shoulders, and the core resisting the pull forward.¦Leaning back to counterbalance; stay stacked.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Ring deadlift\trings\tstrength\t10.0\t\thinge\t0\tglutes, back, legs\tThe 10 lb ring between the feet. Hinge, don\'t squat.\tThe 10 lb ring flat on the floor between the feet, feet hip width.¦Hips back, flat back, reach the ring with both hands, and stand by driving through the heels.¦Hamstrings stretch on the way down; glutes squeeze at the top.¦Squatting down to it; push the hips back and keep the shins still.¦The low back rounds or aches.",
        "Ring goblet squat\trings\tstrength\t10.0\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes, core\tThe 10 lb ring held at the chest. Sit down between the hips, chest tall.\tThe 10 lb ring held at the chest in both hands, feet a little wider than the hips.¦Sit down between the hips, chest tall, pause at the bottom, and stand.¦Thighs and glutes.¦Knees falling inward; think about spreading the floor apart.¦Sharp knee pain.",
        "Ring row\trings\tstrength\t8.0\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tback, arms\tHinge, hold the 8 lb ring, pull it to your hip. The elbow goes back.\tHinge forward with a flat back, the 8 lb ring in one hand hanging under the shoulder.¦Pull the ring to the hip, elbow going back, pause, then lower.¦Beside the shoulder blade on that side.¦Twisting the torso to lift; the shoulders stay square to the floor.¦Low back pain.",
        "Ring overhead press\trings\tstrength\t5.0\t\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tThe 5 lb ring from the chest to straight overhead, slowly.\tThe 5 lb ring held at the chest in both hands, feet hip width, ribs down.¦Press the ring straight overhead slowly, pause, and lower.¦The shoulders; the core keeps the ribs down.¦Leaning back; stay stacked over the hips.¦A pinch at the top of the shoulder.",
        "Ring front raise\trings\tstrength\t5.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders\tThe 5 lb ring in both hands, straight out to eye height.\tThe 5 lb ring held in both hands in front of the thighs.¦Raise it straight out to eye height and lower slowly.¦The front of the shoulders.¦Leaning back; stay tall.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Ring bicep curl\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\taccessory\t0\tarms\tThe 5 lb ring in one hand, elbow pinned to your side. Three counts down.\tThe 5 lb ring in one hand, elbow pinned to the side.¦Curl to the shoulder and lower over three counts.¦The front of that upper arm.¦The elbow drifting forward; pin it.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Ring hammer curl\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\taccessory\t0\tarms\tOne hand through the 5 lb ring, thumb up the whole way. The elbow stays pinned.\tOne hand through the 5 lb ring, thumb up, elbow pinned.¦Curl with the thumb up the whole way and lower slowly.¦The front and outer upper arm and the forearm.¦Turning the palm; it stays thumb-up.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Ring Arnold press\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tThe 5 lb ring at the chin, palm in. Rotate out as you press overhead.\tThe 5 lb ring at the chin in one hand, palm facing you.¦Rotate the palm out as you press overhead, then reverse on the way down.¦All around that shoulder.¦Arching the back on the one-arm version; brace as if both hands were loaded.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Ring behind-back raise\trings\tstrength\t5.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders, back\tBoth hands on the 5 lb ring behind your back. Hinge, then lift it up and away.\tStanding, both hands on the 5 lb ring behind the back, arms long.¦Hinge slightly forward, lift the ring up and away from the body, and lower.¦The back of the shoulders and the chest opening.¦Rounding the shoulders forward; keep the chest open.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Ring half-kneeling overhead hold\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\tcarry\t1\tcore, shoulders\tHalf kneeling, the 5 lb ring held straight overhead in one hand. Shoulders square, ribs stacked.\tHalf kneeling, one knee down, the 5 lb ring held straight overhead in the hand on the same side as the down knee.¦Hold still and breathe, shoulders square, ribs down.¦The shoulder, and the core and the glute of the down leg keeping you upright.¦Leaning away from the ring; stack the ribs over the hips.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Ring triceps extension\trings\tstrength\t8.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tThe 8 lb ring in both hands behind the head, elbows pointing at the ceiling. Only the forearms move.\tThe 8 lb ring in both hands behind the head, elbows pointing at the ceiling.¦Straighten the elbows, pause, and lower.¦The back of the upper arms.¦Elbows drifting out; keep them close.¦Elbow or shoulder pain.",
        "Ring bus driver\trings\tstrength\t5.0\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t0\tshoulders, arms\tThe 5 lb ring held straight out at shoulder height. Turn it like a steering wheel, left and right, slowly.\tThe 5 lb ring held straight out at shoulder height in both hands.¦Turn it like a steering wheel, left and right, slowly.¦The shoulders and the core.¦Letting the arms drop as they tire; lower the weight before the arms do.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Ring wrist curl\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\taccessory\t2\tarms\tSeated, forearm resting along the thigh, the 5 lb ring in that hand. Curl just the wrist, slow both ways.\tSeated, the forearm resting along the thigh with the hand past the knee, the 5 lb ring in that hand.¦Curl only the wrist up, pause, and lower.¦The forearm.¦Lifting the forearm off the thigh; only the wrist moves.¦Wrist pain rather than forearm work.",
        "Ring bridge\trings\tstrength\t10.0\t\tcoreExtension\t2\tglutes\tOn your back, the 10 lb ring resting on the hip bones. Press up through the heels and hold a beat at the top.\tOn your back, knees bent, the 10 lb ring resting on the hip bones held in both hands.¦Press through the heels, lift the hips, hold, and lower.¦The glutes.¦The knees falling out or in; keep them over the feet.¦Low back pain.",
        "Ring chop\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\tcoreAntiRotation\t1\tcore, shoulders\tHalf kneeling, the 5 lb ring at the outside hip. Sweep it slowly up across to the far shoulder, and back down the same line.\tHalf kneeling, the 5 lb ring in both hands at the outside hip of the down knee.¦Sweep it slowly up and across to the far shoulder, then back down the same line.¦The core turning the trunk against a still pelvis.¦The hips rotating with the ring; they face forward the whole time.¦Low back pain.",
        "Ring kickback\trings\tstrength\t5.0\tsides\taccessory\t0\tarms\tHinge, the 5 lb ring in one hand, upper arm parallel to the floor. Straighten the elbow and hold a beat.\tHinge forward with a flat back, the 5 lb ring in one hand, upper arm parallel to the floor.¦Straighten the elbow, hold a beat, and bend.¦The back of that upper arm.¦Dropping the upper arm; keep it level.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Kettlebell deadlift\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\t\thinge\t0\tglutes, back, legs\tThe bell between the feet. Hinge, flat back, stand all the way up.\tFeet under the hips, the bell on the floor between the arches, toes pointing slightly out.¦Push the hips back until the hands reach the handle, grip, then stand by driving the floor away — hips and shoulders rise together.¦The back of the thighs stretch on the way down and the glutes finish the stand.¦Bending the knees first turns it into a squat; lead with the hips and keep the shins nearly vertical.¦The low back rounds or aches rather than the hamstrings working — lighten the bell and hinge less deep.",
        "Kettlebell goblet squat\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes, core\tHeld by the horns at the chest. Sit between the hips, elbows inside the knees.\tThe bell held by the horns at the chest, elbows down, feet a little wider than the hips, toes slightly out.¦Sit straight down between the heels, elbows inside the knees, chest tall, then stand.¦The thighs and glutes doing the work; the bell only asks the core to stay tall.¦The heels lifting or the knees caving in; push the knees out toward the little toes.¦Sharp knee pain on the way down, as opposed to thighs burning.",
        "Kettlebell carry\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tsides\tcarry\t0\tcore, back, arms\tOne hand, ribs stacked over hips, shoulders level. Walk slowly and do not lean.\tThe bell in one hand at the side, standing tall, shoulders level.¦Walk slowly in a straight line, then switch hands; the free arm hangs naturally.¦The side of the trunk opposite the bell working to keep you level, and the grip.¦Leaning away from the bell; stand as if carrying nothing.¦The grip fails before the interval — set it down, shake out, and pick it up again.",
        "Kettlebell around the body\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tdirections\tcoreAntiRotation\t0\tcore\tPass the bell around your waist, hand to hand. The hips stay still; only the arms travel.\tStanding tall, the bell in one hand at the front.¦Pass it around the waist hand to hand in a slow circle, then reverse.¦The core keeping the hips still while the bell travels.¦The hips swaying to meet the bell; only the arms move.¦You cannot pass it without the back twisting — lighten the bell.",
        "Kettlebell row\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tsides\tpullHorizontal\t0\tback, arms\tHinge, free hand braced on your thigh. Pull the bell to your hip; the elbow goes back, not out.\tHinge forward with a flat back, the free hand braced on the thigh, the bell hanging under the shoulder.¦Pull the bell to the hip, elbow going back not out, pause, then lower slowly.¦The muscles beside the shoulder blade; the arm is just the handle.¦Shrugging the shoulder toward the ear; keep it down and pull with the back.¦The low back aches from holding the hinge — rest it, then hinge less deep.",
        "Kettlebell sumo squat\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes\tFeet wide, toes out, the bell hanging in both hands. Sit straight down between the heels, chest tall.\tFeet wide, toes turned out, the bell hanging in both hands between the legs.¦Sit straight down between the heels, chest up, then drive through the feet to stand.¦The inner thighs and glutes.¦Leaning forward so the bell swings; keep the torso tall and the bell hanging straight down.¦Knee or groin pain that is sharp, not a stretch.",
        "Kettlebell rack hold\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tsides\tcarry\t0\tcore, arms, shoulders\tThe bell resting on the forearm, fist at the collarbone, elbow tucked. Stand tall and breathe; ribs stay down.\tThe bell resting on the forearm with the fist at the collarbone, elbow tucked to the ribs.¦Stand tall and breathe; the bell does not move.¦The core holding you upright against the weight on one side.¦The elbow winging out so the bell hangs on the wrist; keep it tucked.¦Wrist pain — adjust the bell deeper into the hand.",
        "Kickstand deadlift\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tsides\thinge\t0\tglutes, legs, back\tThe bell inside the front foot, back toes down just for balance. Hinge over the front leg, flat back.\tThe bell inside the front foot; the back foot a step behind with only the toes down, like a kickstand.¦Hinge over the front leg, hips back, reach the bell, and stand through the front heel.¦The front hamstring and glute do nearly all of it; the back foot only balances.¦Loading the back foot makes it a split squat; keep nine tenths of your weight on the front leg.¦The front knee caves inward or the low back takes the load.",
        "Kettlebell suitcase hold\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\tsides\tcarry\t0\tcore, arms\tThe bell in one hand at your side. Stand level — no lean — and let the grip do the work.\tThe bell in one hand at the side, feet hip width.¦Stand perfectly level and breathe; nothing moves.¦The side of the trunk opposite the bell, and the grip.¦A lean toward or away from the weight; check that the shoulders are level.¦Grip failure; set it down and rest.",
        "Kettlebell calf raise\tkettlebell\tstrength\t18.0\t\taccessory\t0\tlegs\tThe bell in one hand, the other hand on the wall. Rise to the balls of the feet, pause, lower slowly.\tStanding tall, the bell in one hand, the other hand on a wall for balance.¦Rise onto the balls of the feet, pause at the top, and lower slowly.¦The calves.¦Bouncing; pause at the top and lower over two counts.¦Achilles pain.",
        "Dumbbell press\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tTwo pounds is enough when you go slowly.\tStanding tall, a dumbbell in each hand at the shoulders, palms forward, ribs down.¦Press straight up until the arms are by the ears, then lower slowly to the shoulders.¦The shoulders and the back of the arms.¦Arching the low back to push the weight up; brace the core and keep the ribs down.¦A pinch at the top of the shoulder.",
        "Lateral raise\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders\tUp to shoulder height, down over three counts.\tStanding tall, light dumbbells at the sides, elbows very slightly bent.¦Raise the arms out to the sides to shoulder height, lead with the elbows, and lower over three counts.¦The tops of the shoulders.¦Shrugging or swinging; if you need to swing, the weight is too heavy.¦A pinch at the top of the shoulder — stop a little below shoulder height.",
        "Front raise\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders\tStraight arms to eye height. Stop before the shoulders shrug.\tStanding tall, dumbbells in front of the thighs, arms straight.¦Raise the arms straight out in front to eye height and lower slowly.¦The front of the shoulders.¦Swinging the body; stop before the shoulders shrug.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Rear delt fly\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tshoulders, back\tHinge forward, open wide, squeeze between the shoulder blades.\tHinge forward with a flat back, a light dumbbell in each hand hanging below the chest, palms facing each other.¦Open the arms wide with soft elbows until they are level with the shoulders, squeeze, and lower.¦The back of the shoulders and between the blades.¦Swinging the weights up; they should be light enough to move slowly.¦A pinch in the front of the shoulder.",
        "Arnold press\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tPalms in at the chin, rotate out as you press up.\tDumbbells at the chin, palms facing you, elbows in front.¦Rotate the palms outward as you press overhead, then reverse on the way down.¦All around the shoulders.¦Rushing the rotation; it happens through the whole press, not at the top.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Bicep curl\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tElbows pinned to your sides. Three counts down every time.\tStanding tall, a dumbbell in each hand, elbows pinned to the sides.¦Curl to the shoulders and lower over three counts; only the forearms move.¦The front of the upper arms.¦Swinging the body or the elbows drifting forward; pin them.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Tricep kickback\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tUpper arm still and parallel to the floor. Only the forearm moves.\tHinge forward with a flat back, a dumbbell in each hand, upper arms parallel to the floor.¦Straighten the elbows until the arms are long, squeeze, and bend again; the upper arm stays still.¦The back of the upper arms.¦The upper arm swinging to help; it does not move.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Floor fly\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t2\tchest\tOn your back, soft elbows, open until the arms touch the floor.\tOn your back, knees bent, a light dumbbell in each hand above the chest, palms facing, elbows soft.¦Open the arms wide until they touch the floor, then bring them back together over the chest.¦A stretch across the chest, then the chest closing the arms.¦Bending the elbows to make it a press; the angle at the elbow does not change.¦Shoulder pain at the bottom.",
        "Around the world\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders, chest\tArms wide, sweep overhead until they meet, and back the same way.\tStanding tall, light dumbbells at the sides, palms forward.¦Sweep the straight arms out and up until they meet overhead, then back down the same path.¦The shoulders all the way around.¦Bending the elbows or arching the back; keep both long and the ribs down.¦Shoulder pinch — it is fine to stop the sweep below the top.",
        "Dumbbell shrug\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tback, shoulders\tShoulders straight up toward the ears, hold a beat, then let them go.\tStanding tall, dumbbells at the sides.¦Lift the shoulders straight up toward the ears, hold a beat, and let them down.¦The top of the shoulders and neck.¦Rolling the shoulders in a circle; straight up and down only.¦Neck pain.",
        "Upright row\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpullVertical\t0\tshoulders, back\tHands apart, elbows lead wide, no higher than the chest. Stop before the shoulders shrug.\tStanding tall, dumbbells in front of the thighs, hands a little apart.¦Lead with the elbows wide, lifting the weights no higher than the chest, then lower.¦The tops of the shoulders.¦Lifting past the chest, which pinches the shoulder; stop at chest height.¦Any pinch at the front or top of the shoulder — this move is not for everyone, and skipping it is fine.",
        "Overhead extension\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tBoth hands on one weight behind the head. Only the forearms move.\tStanding tall, both hands on one dumbbell held behind the head, elbows pointing at the ceiling.¦Straighten the elbows to press it overhead, then lower slowly behind the head.¦The back of the upper arms.¦The elbows flaring wide; keep them pointing up and close to the head.¦Elbow or shoulder pain.",
        "Pullover\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpullVertical\t2\tchest, back, core\tOn your back, one weight held in both hands, arms straight. Take it back past your head only as far as the ribs stay down.\tOn your back, knees bent, one dumbbell held in both hands above the chest, arms straight but not locked.¦Take the weight back past the head as far as the ribs stay down, then bring it back over the chest.¦The back under the armpits and the chest stretching.¦Letting the ribs flare and the low back arch; keep the ribs down the whole way.¦Shoulder pain at the bottom — shorten the range.",
        "Boxer punches\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t0\tshoulders, arms, core\tAlternating, chest height, controlled. The shoulders do the work.\tStanding, light dumbbells at the chest, knees soft, one foot slightly forward.¦Punch one arm straight out at chest height and draw it back as the other goes, controlled, not fast.¦The shoulders and chest; the core turning slightly with each punch.¦Locking the elbow at the end of the punch; stop just short.¦Elbow or shoulder pain.",
        "Raise the platters\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms, shoulders\tPalms up at the waist, as if carrying two platters. Extend the arms forward, lift to shoulder height, and lower over three counts.\tStanding tall, dumbbells at the waist, palms up as if carrying two platters.¦Extend the arms forward, lift to shoulder height, and bring them back the same way.¦The front of the shoulders and the biceps.¦Letting the palms turn in; they stay up.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Tricep press-back\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tArms straight at your sides, palms facing behind you. Press the weights back and up, and hold a beat at the top.\tStanding tall, dumbbells at the sides, palms facing behind you, arms straight.¦Press the weights back and up, hold a beat, and return.¦The back of the upper arms and the back of the shoulders.¦Leaning forward to swing them higher; stay tall and keep it small.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Dumbbell floor press\tdumbbells\tstrength\t5.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t2\tchest, arms\tOn your back, a 5 lb dumbbell in each hand. Press straight up; the floor catches your elbows between reps.\tOn your back, knees bent, a dumbbell in each hand, upper arms on the floor, forearms vertical.¦Press straight up until the arms are long, then lower until the upper arms rest on the floor.¦Chest and the back of the arms.¦Flaring the elbows straight out to the sides; keep them at about forty-five degrees.¦A pinch in the front of the shoulder.",
        "Dumbbell row\tdumbbells\tstrength\t5.0\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tback, arms\tHinge and hold it there. Pull both 5 lb dumbbells to your hips, blades together at the top.\tHinge forward with a flat back, a dumbbell in each hand hanging under the shoulders.¦Pull both to the hips, blades together at the top, and lower over three counts.¦Between the shoulder blades.¦Elbows flaring wide; they go back, close to the body.¦Low back pain.",
        "Zottman curl\tdumbbells\tstrength\t3.0\t\taccessory\t0\tarms\tCurl palms up, turn palms down at the top, lower over three counts. The way down is the point.\tStanding tall, dumbbells at the sides, palms forward.¦Curl up palms up, turn the palms down at the top, and lower slowly over three counts.¦The front of the arms up, the forearms down.¦Rushing the lowering; the way down is the point.¦Wrist or elbow pain.",
        "Scaption raise\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\taccessory\t0\tshoulders\tStraight arms, thumbs up, lifted halfway between front and side. To shoulder height and no higher.\tStanding tall, dumbbells at the sides, thumbs up.¦Raise the straight arms halfway between front and side to shoulder height, and lower.¦The shoulders and the muscles around the blade.¦Going above shoulder height; stop there.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Squeeze press\tdumbbells\tstrength\t3.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t0\tchest, arms\tPress the two weights together hard at the chest, then press them to the ceiling without letting them part.\tStanding or lying, two dumbbells pressed hard together at the chest, palms facing.¦Keep squeezing them together while pressing away from the chest, then return without letting them part.¦The inner chest.¦Letting the dumbbells separate; the squeeze is the move.¦Shoulder or wrist pain.",
        "Dumbbell dead bug press\tdumbbells\tstrength\t2.0\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore, shoulders\tA dead bug with the dumbbells pressed to the ceiling. Low back flat, arms straight the whole time.\tAs the dead bug, with a light dumbbell in each hand pressed to the ceiling.¦Lower one leg slowly while the arms stay pressed up and still, then switch.¦The deep abdominals and the shoulders holding the weights steady.¦The arms drifting overhead as the leg lowers; they stay over the chest.¦The low back lifts off the floor.",
        "Russian twist\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tcoreFlexion\t2\tcore\tSeated tall, knees bent, the dumbbell in both hands. Turn from the ribs, side to side, slowly — the chest stays lifted the whole time.\tSeated, knees bent, heels on the floor, leaning back slightly with a tall spine, the dumbbell in both hands at the chest.¦Turn from the ribs to one side, then the other, slowly; the weight follows the chest.¦The sides of the trunk.¦Swinging the arms while the chest stays facing forward; the ribs turn and the arms go along.¦Low back pain — sit taller and reduce the lean.",
        "Standing side bend\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\tsides\tcoreFlexion\t0\tcore\tThe dumbbell in one hand, slide it down the outside of the thigh and stand tall again.\tStanding tall, the dumbbell in one hand at the side, feet hip width.¦Slide the weight down the outside of the thigh, bending only sideways, then stand tall.¦The side of the trunk opposite the weight pulling you back up.¦Leaning forward or back; the movement is in one plane, straight to the side.¦Low back pain.",
        "Dumbbell march\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tcarry\t0\tcore\tThe dumbbell in both hands at your chest. March slowly; the ribs stay stacked over the hips.\tThe dumbbell in both hands at the chest, standing tall.¦March slowly, lifting each knee to hip height, ribs stacked over the hips.¦The core holding you still while the legs move.¦Leaning back to lift the knee; stay tall.¦Low back ache.",
        "Suitcase deadlift\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\tsides\thinge\t0\tglutes, legs, core\tThe dumbbell beside one foot. Hinge, take a firm grip, and stand tall — no lean toward the load.\tThe dumbbell on the floor beside one foot, feet hip width, shoulders level.¦Hinge, grip, and stand tall without leaning toward the weight; then lower it the same way.¦The hamstrings on the way down, and the side of the trunk opposite the weight holding you level.¦Tipping sideways toward the load; the whole point is to stay square.¦You cannot stay level without the low back twisting.",
        "Tall-kneeling press\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tpushVertical\t1\tshoulders, core, arms\tKneeling tall, the dumbbell in both hands at the chest. Press it overhead; ribs down, hips under you.\tKneeling tall on both knees, hips forward, the dumbbell in both hands at the chest.¦Press it overhead with the ribs down and the glutes tight, then lower.¦Shoulders, and the glutes and core holding you upright.¦Sitting back onto the heels or arching; squeeze the glutes and stay tall.¦Knee discomfort on the floor — kneel on a folded towel.",
        "Plank pull-through\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore, shoulders\tFrom a high plank, drag the dumbbell under your chest to the other side, hand by hand. The hips stay quiet.\tA high plank with the dumbbell on the floor just outside one hand, feet wide.¦Reach under the chest with the far hand, drag the weight across to the other side, and repeat the other way.¦The core holding the hips square as one hand leaves the floor.¦The hips twisting toward the ceiling; keep them level.¦Wrist or low back pain.",
        "Single-dumbbell row\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\tsides\tpullHorizontal\t0\tback, arms\tHinge, free hand braced on your thigh, the dumbbell in the other. Pull it to your hip; the elbow goes back, not out.\tHinge forward with a flat back, a dumbbell in each hand hanging under the shoulders.¦Pull both to the hips, blades together at the top, and lower over three counts.¦Between the shoulder blades.¦Elbows flaring wide; they go back, close to the body.¦Low back pain.",
        "Single-dumbbell goblet squat\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes, core\tThe dumbbell held upright at the chest in both hands. Sit between the hips, elbows inside the knees.\tThe bell held by the horns at the chest, elbows down, feet a little wider than the hips, toes slightly out.¦Sit straight down between the heels, elbows inside the knees, chest tall, then stand.¦The thighs and glutes doing the work; the bell only asks the core to stay tall.¦The heels lifting or the knees caving in; push the knees out toward the little toes.¦Sharp knee pain on the way down, as opposed to thighs burning.",
        "Single-dumbbell floor press\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\t\tpushHorizontal\t2\tchest, arms\tOn your back, the dumbbell in both hands over the chest. Press straight up; the floor stops your elbows.\tOn your back, knees bent, a dumbbell in each hand, upper arms on the floor, forearms vertical.¦Press straight up until the arms are long, then lower until the upper arms rest on the floor.¦Chest and the back of the arms.¦Flaring the elbows straight out to the sides; keep them at about forty-five degrees.¦A pinch in the front of the shoulder.",
        "Single-dumbbell overhead press\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\tsides\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tThe dumbbell in one hand at the shoulder. Press straight up, ribs down; the free hand on the hip.\tStanding tall, a dumbbell in each hand at the shoulders, palms forward, ribs down.¦Press straight up until the arms are by the ears, then lower slowly to the shoulders.¦The shoulders and the back of the arms.¦Arching the low back to push the weight up; brace the core and keep the ribs down.¦A pinch at the top of the shoulder.",
        "Single-dumbbell curl\tsingleDumbbell\tstrength\t10.0\tsides\taccessory\t0\tarms\tThe dumbbell in one hand, elbow pinned to your side. Three counts down every time.\tStanding tall, a dumbbell in each hand, elbows pinned to the sides.¦Curl to the shoulders and lower over three counts; only the forearms move.¦The front of the upper arms.¦Swinging the body or the elbows drifting forward; pin them.¦Elbow pain.",
        "Band pull-apart\tband\tstrength\t\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tshoulders, back\tArms straight at shoulder height, pull the band to your chest. Blades together, then let it close slowly.\tThe band held in both hands at shoulder height, arms straight, hands shoulder width.¦Pull the hands apart until the band touches the chest, squeeze the blades, and let it return slowly.¦Between the shoulder blades.¦Shrugging; keep the shoulders down.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Band face pull\tband\tstrength\t\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tshoulders, back\tPull the band toward your eyes, elbows high and wide, thumbs turning back. The shoulder blades finish it.\tThe band anchored or held in front at face height, hands together.¦Pull toward the eyes with the elbows high and wide, thumbs turning back, then return slowly.¦The back of the shoulders.¦Pulling to the chest instead of the face; keep the elbows high.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Band W raise\tband\tstrength\t\t\tpullHorizontal\t0\tshoulders, back\tElbows bent to a W, band between the hands. Draw the elbows down and back until the blades meet.\tElbows bent and tucked, the band between the hands, forearms making a W.¦Draw the elbows down and back until the shoulder blades squeeze, then release.¦Between and below the shoulder blades.¦Arching the low back to help; keep the ribs down.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Band external rotation\tband\tstrength\t\tsides\taccessory\t0\tshoulders\tElbow pinned at your side, forearm swings out against the band. Slow out, slower back.\tElbow pinned to the side at ninety degrees, the band held across the body.¦Swing the forearm outward against the band, slowly, and slower back.¦The back of the shoulder, deep.¦The elbow leaving the side; pin it.¦Shoulder pain.",
        "Band seated row\tband\tstrength\t\t\tpullHorizontal\t2\tback, arms\tSeated, legs long, the band looped around both feet. Pull to the ribs, blades together, let it return slowly.\tSeated on the floor, legs long, the band looped around both feet, handles in the hands.¦Pull to the ribs with the elbows close, blades together, then let the arms out slowly.¦Between the shoulder blades.¦Rounding the back as the arms go out; sit tall the whole way.¦Low back pain.",
        "Band overhead press\tband\tstrength\t\t\tpushVertical\t0\tshoulders, arms\tStand on the middle of the band, an end in each hand at the shoulders. Press up against it, slower on the way down.\tStanding on the middle of the band, an end in each hand at the shoulders.¦Press up against the band until the arms are straight, then lower under control.¦Shoulders.¦Leaning back against the tension; keep the ribs down.¦Shoulder pinch.",
        "Chin tuck\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\taccessory\t0\tback, core\tDraw the chin straight back — yes, a double chin. Hold two counts, release. Eyes level the whole time.\tSitting or standing tall, eyes level, shoulders relaxed.¦Draw the chin straight back as if making a double chin, hold two counts, and release.¦The front of the neck working and the back of the neck lengthening.¦Tipping the head down; the eyes stay level and the head glides back.¦Dizziness or sharp neck pain.",
        "Wall angel\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tpullVertical\t0\tshoulders, back, core\tBack, head and arms against the wall. Slide the arms up and down; ribs down, nothing leaves the wall.\tBack, head and arms flat against a wall, elbows bent to ninety degrees, feet a step out.¦Slide the arms up the wall and back down, keeping wrists, elbows and the low back touching.¦The muscles between the shoulder blades working, and the chest stretching.¦The ribs lifting off the wall to reach higher; go only as high as the back stays flat.¦A sharp pinch in the shoulder.",
        "Dead bug\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore\tRibs down, low back flat on the floor.\tOn your back, arms straight up over the chest, knees over the hips at ninety degrees, low back pressed into the floor.¦Lower one arm overhead and the opposite leg toward the floor, slowly, then return and switch.¦The deep abdominals working to keep the low back flat.¦The low back arching off the floor; go only as far as it stays pressed down.¦The back lifts on every rep — shorten the range or move one limb at a time.",
        "Incline push-up\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tpushHorizontal\t0\tchest, arms, core\tHands on the counter. The higher the hands, the easier it is.\tHands on a counter or sturdy surface a little wider than the shoulders, body in one straight line from head to heels.¦Lower the chest toward the surface with the elbows at about forty-five degrees, then press back up.¦Chest and the back of the arms; the core holds the line.¦Hips sagging or piking up; squeeze the glutes and keep one straight line.¦A pinch in the front of the shoulder or wrist pain — raise the hands higher.",
        "Reverse lunge\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\tlunge\t0\tlegs, glutes\tStep back, not forward. The front knee stays over the ankle.\tStanding tall, feet under the hips, hands on the hips or at the chest.¦Step one foot back, lower until the back knee nearly touches the floor, and push through the front heel to return.¦The front thigh and glute; the back leg only steadies you.¦Stepping forward instead, which loads the knee; step back, and keep the front knee over the ankle.¦Sharp pain in the front knee.",
        "Glute bridge\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreExtension\t2\tglutes\tHeels close, press through them, hold a beat at the top.\tOn your back, knees bent, heels close to the hips, arms by the sides.¦Press through the heels to lift the hips until the body is a straight line from knees to shoulders, hold, and lower slowly.¦The glutes, with a little hamstring.¦Arching the low back to go higher; stop where the glutes are doing it.¦Hamstring cramp — walk the heels a little further away.",
        "Split squat\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\tlunge\t0\tlegs, glutes\tBack knee straight down. Most of the weight on the front foot.\tOne foot forward, one back, a long stride apart, most of your weight on the front foot.¦Lower the back knee straight down toward the floor, then stand; the feet stay where they are.¦Front thigh and glute.¦Leaning forward over the front knee; keep the torso upright and the hips square.¦Sharp knee pain.",
        "Bird dog\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore, back\tOpposite arm and leg, slowly. The hips do not tip.\tOn all fours, hands under the shoulders, knees under the hips, back flat.¦Reach one arm forward and the opposite leg back until both are long and level, pause, and return.¦The core holding the hips still; the glute of the reaching leg.¦The hips tipping as the leg lifts; keep them square to the floor.¦Low back or wrist pain.",
        "Wall sit\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs\tThighs parallel if you can, higher if you cannot. Breathe.\tBack flat against the wall, feet a step out, hip width.¦Slide down until the thighs are parallel to the floor, or higher if they cannot be, and hold.¦The front of the thighs burning; that is the whole move.¦Hands on the thighs; they rest by your sides or across the chest.¦Knee pain behind the kneecap rather than thigh burn.",
        "Forearm plank\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore\tElbows under the shoulders, one straight line from head to heels. Breathe, don\'t sag.\tForearms on the floor, elbows under the shoulders, toes tucked, one straight line from head to heels.¦Hold and breathe normally; nothing moves.¦The whole front of the trunk, and the glutes if you squeeze them.¦Hips sagging or lifting; squeeze the glutes to find the line.¦Low back ache — lower the knees to the floor and hold from there.",
        "Side plank\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore\tOn one forearm, feet stacked or staggered. Lift the hips and hold them still.\tOn one forearm, elbow under the shoulder, feet stacked or the top foot in front, body in a line.¦Lift the hips until the body is straight and hold still.¦The side of the trunk nearest the floor.¦The hips dropping back or sagging; think of being pressed between two panes of glass.¦Shoulder pain — drop to the knee version.",
        "Lying leg raise\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreFlexion\t2\tcore\tLow back pressed into the floor. Lower the legs only as far as it stays there.\tOn your back, legs long, hands under the hips or by the sides, low back pressed into the floor.¦Lift the legs to vertical and lower them only as far as the low back stays down.¦The lower abdominals.¦Lowering past the point the back arches; bend the knees to shorten the lever.¦Low back pain on the way down.",
        "Bicycle crunch\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreFlexion\t2\tcore\tSlow. Opposite elbow toward opposite knee, and the straight leg reaches long.\tOn your back, hands lightly behind the head, knees up.¦Bring one elbow toward the opposite knee while the other leg reaches long, then switch, slowly.¦The abdominals, especially the sides.¦Pulling on the neck; the hands only rest there, and the elbows stay wide.¦Neck strain.",
        "Plank shoulder tap\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore, shoulders\tFrom a high plank, tap the opposite shoulder. The hips stay square to the floor.\tA high plank on the hands, feet a little wider than the hips for balance.¦Lift one hand and tap the opposite shoulder, set it down, and switch, slowly.¦The core working to keep the hips from rocking.¦The hips swinging side to side; go slower and widen the feet.¦Wrist pain — turn the hands out slightly or make fists.",
        "Superman\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreExtension\t2\tback, glutes, core\tOn your belly, arms reaching long. Float the arms and legs an inch off the mat and hold; keep looking down.\tOn your belly, arms reaching long in front, legs long behind, forehead toward the floor.¦Float the arms and legs an inch off the mat, hold, and lower.¦The whole back of the body working gently.¦Lifting high and craning the neck; keep it small and the gaze down.¦Low back pain rather than muscle work.",
        "One-leg bridge\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\tcoreExtension\t2\tglutes, legs\tOne foot planted, the other leg held long or hugged in. Press through the heel; the hips stay level.\tAs the glute bridge, with one foot planted and the other leg held long or hugged in.¦Press through the planted heel and lift the hips level, then lower.¦The glute of the planted leg.¦The hips tipping toward the lifted leg; keep them level.¦Hamstring cramp or low back pain.",
        "Single-leg calf raise\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\taccessory\t0\tlegs\tAll your weight on one foot, fingertips on the wall. Rise to the ball of the foot, pause, lower with control.\tAll your weight on one foot, fingertips on a wall.¦Rise onto the ball of that foot, pause, and lower slowly.¦That calf.¦Rolling onto the outside of the foot; rise through the big toe.¦Achilles pain.",
        "Side leg lift\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\tsides\taccessory\t2\tglutes\tSide lying, bottom knee bent, top leg long. Lift to hip height, no higher, and lower slowly.\tLying on one side, bottom knee bent for balance, top leg long, hips stacked.¦Lift the top leg to hip height, no higher, and lower slowly.¦The outer hip of the top leg.¦Rolling the hip back so the leg comes forward; keep the hips stacked and the toes pointing forward.¦Hip pinch.",
        "Bear hold\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreAntiRotation\t2\tcore, shoulders\tOn all fours, toes tucked, knees hovering an inch off the mat. Flat back, and breathe.\tOn all fours, toes tucked, hands under the shoulders.¦Lift the knees an inch off the floor and hold, back flat, breathing.¦The whole core and the front of the thighs.¦The back rounding or the hips rising; keep the knees low and the back flat.¦Wrist pain.",
        "Air squat\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tsquat\t0\tlegs, glutes\tFeet under the hips, sit down and back, chest tall. Stand all the way up every time.\tFeet under the hips or a little wider, toes slightly out, arms out in front for balance.¦Sit down and back as if to a chair, chest tall, as low as your heels stay down, then stand all the way up.¦Thighs and glutes.¦Heels rising or knees caving; slow down and let the knees track over the toes.¦Sharp knee pain.",
        "Reverse tabletop hold\tbodyweight\tstrength\t\t\tcoreExtension\t2\tarms, shoulders, glutes\tSeated, hands behind you, fingers toward your heels. Press the hips up level with the knees and hold, chest broad.\tSeated, hands behind you with the fingers pointing toward the heels, feet flat.¦Press the hips up until level with the knees and hold, chest open.¦The glutes, the back of the shoulders and the back of the arms.¦The hips sagging; press them up and squeeze the glutes.¦Wrist or shoulder pain.",
        "Lymphatic bounce\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tSoft knees, heels barely leaving the floor. Loose everywhere above the waist.\t",
        "Arm swings\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tLet the arms swing across the body and wrap. The waist turns, the arms are heavy.\t",
        "Shoulder rolls\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tBig and slow, back rather than forward. Let the breath set the pace.\t",
        "Neck release\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tEar toward shoulder, then slowly across. Never roll back through the neck.\t",
        "Spinal wave\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tMove one vertebra at a time, tailbone to head and back down.\t",
        "Hip circles\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tHands on the hips, wide slow circles. Both directions, evenly.\t",
        "Cat cow\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOn all fours. Arch on the breath in, round on the breath out.\t",
        "Lymphatic tapping\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tLight cupped taps: collarbones, under the arms, then down the inside of the legs.\t",
        "Standing twist\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tFeet planted, turn from the middle. The arms follow rather than lead.\t",
        "Ankle and wrist circles\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tSmall, slow, both directions. The joints furthest out get the least attention.\t",
        "Forward fold hang\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tKnees soft, hang from the hips. Let the head be heavy.\t",
        "Chest opener\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tArms wide and back, chest lifting. Let the breath in do the opening.\t",
        "Standing march\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tKnee to hip height, slowly. The foot goes down before the next one lifts.\t",
        "Arm circles\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tBig and slow, both directions. The shoulder does the work, not the elbow.\t",
        "Deep squat hold\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tSit as low as is comfortable, heels down if they reach. Breathe there.\t",
        "Ankle rocking\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tRock forward onto the toes, then back onto the heels. Small and slow.\t",
        "Corkscrew\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tArms out to the sides at shoulder height. Twist them in place, palms turning over and back.\t",
        "Allen wrench\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tBoth elbows bent square — one arm up, one down. Rotate back and forth, swapping which is which.\t",
        "Vertical arm swings\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOne arm swings up overhead as the other swings down past the hip. They alternate, long and loose.\t",
        "Bent-over trunk twists\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tHinge forward with a flat back, arms wide, and rotate one shoulder toward the floor and back.\t",
        "Slam dunks\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tBoth arms overhead, then drive them down past the hips together and with intent. The knees give a little.\t",
        "Golf swings\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tHands together, swing low across the body and up over the far shoulder. Both directions.\t",
        "High knee circles\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOne knee up to hip height, then circle it out and away. Slow, and both legs.\t",
        "Thread the needle\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOn all fours, slide one arm beneath the other and let that shoulder rest toward the floor. Unwind slowly, then the other side.\t",
        "Child\'s pose reach\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tKneel back toward the heels, arms long on the mat. Walk the hands to one side, breathe there, then the other.\t",
        "Knee sways\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOn your back, knees bent, feet a little wide. Let both knees fall to one side, then the other, at the pace of the breath.\t",
        "Sun breath\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tSweep the arms wide and overhead on the breath in, float them down on the breath out. Nothing to hurry.\t",
        "Pelvic rocks\tbodyweight\tflow\t\t\t\t\t\tOn your back, knees bent. Tip the pelvis toward you and away, small and slow; the low back presses and releases.\t",
    ]
}
